The safe source-splicing path refuses this edit instead of printing the
expected document. Removing the blockquote brings an indented code block next
to a list; CommonMark then parses the code as part of the final list item.

What it should do: remove only the selected block and keep the formerly
separate indented code block separate, without rewriting that untouched code.

Cause: blank lines alone cannot terminate the list before an indented code
block. The source editor detects the block-count loss and refuses the edit,
but a lossless representation for this new boundary is not yet implemented.

Why it matters: accepting the naive splice silently changes the structure of
an untouched block. Refusal is safer, but the requested removal still cannot
be completed.
